;; karakuri (絡繰) service capability + ToS registry — :representative (R0, G8).
;; Each record drives adapter-tier selection (T1 official-API preferred) and the G2 ToS gate.
;; TWO independent stance axes (a service can sanction its API yet forbid browser automation —
;; Google + Facebook are exactly that case):
;;   :service/tos-stance — the OFFICIAL-API stance (:api-ok …); governs T1 selection.
;;   :service/t2-stance  — the BROWSER-AUTOMATION stance (:permitted / :restricted / :prohibited);
;;                         a :prohibited t2-stance refuses the T2 headless-browser adapter by
;;                         construction (G2), EVEN when an official API exists.
;;   :service/t2-engine  — the browser-automation engine for a T2-eligible service: :browser-use
;;                         (a LangGraph-driven browser agent over Playwright). Present ONLY where the
;;                         t2-stance permits automation; absent where it is :prohibited.
;; This is policy/capability data, NOT an endorsement. karakuri drives only the MEMBER's OWN account
;; (G1) and holds no credential (G3). ToS stances are :representative and MUST be operator-verified
;; before any live use (G6); a vendor can change its ToS at any time.
[{:service/id "squarespace"
  :service/name "Squarespace"
  :service/category :site-builder
  :service/official-api true
  :service/auth-model :oauth2
  :service/tos-stance :api-ok
  :service/t2-stance :prohibited
  :service/tier :t1-official-api
  :service/rate-limit "documented per-endpoint; backoff on 429"
  :service/representative true}

